From 9511abbb5b7603721af83ce1e849631a313e3793 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Witold=20Bo=C5=82t?= <witold.bolt@jit.team>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 20:05:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] v3d: decline HW mipmap-gen for NPOT textures (fixes
 scrambled Q2 model skins on Pi4)

The TFU multi-level mipmap generator supplies OPAD only for level 0 and infers
the tiling of levels >=1 internally; that inference only matches
v3d_setup_slices / the TMU sampler for power-of-two bases. NPOT bases (with
ub_pad + pot_width/pot_height padding on the small UBLINEAR/LINEARTILE levels)
get a generated layout that diverges from the sampled layout, so distant NPOT
textures (Quake II model skins: banner 260x195, gibs, soldier 288x195...) read
as garbage while the base level and all POT textures render correctly.

Decline NPOT in v3d_generate_mipmap so st_generate_mipmap falls back to the
render-based util_gen_mipmap path (per-level-correct surfaces). POT keeps the
fast TFU path (no-op guard).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit e4be1163240fe63c3892744cb3d815f9603a9fdc)
---
 src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3d_blit.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3d_blit.c b/src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3d_blit.c
index c5c07d1deb0..68c38ad1092 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3d_blit.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3d_blit.c
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
 #include "util/perf/cpu_trace.h"
 #include "util/u_surface.h"
 #include "util/u_blitter.h"
+#include "util/bitscan.h"
 #include "compiler/nir/nir_builder.h"
 #include "v3d_context.h"
 #include "broadcom/common/v3d_tiling.h"
@@ -252,6 +253,21 @@ v3d_generate_mipmap(struct pipe_context *pctx,
         if (prsc->target == PIPE_TEXTURE_3D)
                 return false;
 
+        /* Phoenix/RPi4 workaround (Quake II NPOT model skins rendered scrambled
+         * at distance): the TFU multi-level mipmap generator supplies OPAD only
+         * for level 0 and INFERS the tiling of levels >=1 internally. That
+         * inference only matches what v3d_setup_slices/the TMU sampler
+         * reconstruct when the base dimensions are powers of two; for NPOT bases
+         * (which carry ub_pad and pot_width/pot_height padding on the small
+         * UBLINEAR/LINEARTILE levels) the generated layout diverges from the
+         * sampled layout, so those mip levels read as garbage. Decline NPOT here
+         * so st_generate_mipmap falls back to the render-based util_gen_mipmap
+         * path, which lays out each level via its own correctly-tiled surface.
+         * POT textures keep the fast TFU path (this guard is a no-op for them). */
+        if (!util_is_power_of_two_or_zero(prsc->width0) ||
+            !util_is_power_of_two_or_zero(prsc->height0))
+                return false;
+
         struct v3d_context *v3d = v3d_context(pctx);
         struct v3d_screen *screen = v3d->screen;
         struct v3d_device_info *devinfo = &screen->devinfo;
